Patient, female 56 years old. The disease debuted in 2015, 1
month after radioiodine therapy for thyrotoxicosis, episodes of
stiffness and pain in the muscles of the back. Since March 2018, the
patient noted an increase in the stiffness of the axial muscles, fear of
walking, and began to use a cane. In May 2018, constant muscular
activity in EMG in paraspinal muscles, proximal muscles of the
thighs, an increase of anti-GAD antibodies to 46 U/ml, diagnosed
Stiff-person syndrome..
